          acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "They solve different halves of the problem. A battery backup switches over automatically within seconds, works when nobody is home, and needs no fuel — but typically runs a pump for hours rather than days. A generator can run indefinitely on fuel but requires a person to start it, place it safely and refuel it. For flood protection specifically, the battery is the more reliable protection and the generator is the endurance." },
