        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can a portable power station run a sump pump?",
          acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "Some can, but check two things: continuous output capacity against the pump's surge draw, and whether the inverter produces a pure sine wave, since induction motors dislike modified sine wave power. A unit rated around 2,000 watts with a surge allowance will typically start a half-horsepower pump. Runtime depends on capacity, and intermittent pumping stretches it considerably." },
        },
