        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Buy the battery backup first.</strong> It is the only option that protects the basement automatically at three in the morning or while you are away, and it also covers a primary pump that has simply failed with the power still on.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Add the generator for endurance and for everything else in the house. A 2,000 watt machine runs the pump alone; 3,500 to 5,000 covers the pump, the furnace blower, the fridge and lighting. Size for simultaneous starting surges, not running watts.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then test both, on a schedule, because a dead battery and an unstarted generator fail exactly the same way — silently, at the moment the water starts rising.
          </p>
